{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-014", "category": "ordinary_tutorial", "context_hash": "0c413931f240e61846349ce777d58c8d298239f071b8167f028fc23f296b044b", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|What Gmsh is pretty good at|paragraph|a05b3c618eb8fd534106187dfdd9e3eb4671635acb62662fbcc2c27a2abda398", "msgid": "visualize and export computational results in a great variety of\nways. Gmsh can display scalar, vector and tensor datasets, perform\nvarious operations on the resulting post-processing views\n(@pxref{Post-processing module}), can export plots in many different\nformats, and can generate complex animations (see e.g. @ref{t8});", "msgid_sha256": "a05b3c618eb8fd534106187dfdd9e3eb4671635acb62662fbcc2c27a2abda398", "node": "What Gmsh is pretty good at", "protected_hash": "7ce8a38a8f6f03c7db864b6718733d224c488d55adf139f19c1cdae43a4ceac2", "protected_values": ["@pxref{Post-processing module}", "@ref{t8}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "0e1d8c38b2f325d9798966659bbf72c74b5cbef6dca3ece5894f7a46555c501a", "semantic_key": "a05b3c618eb8fd534106187dfdd9e3eb4671635acb62662fbcc2c27a2abda398", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "1987eb3fff838ae598bd337f7ac0ce6f033b89c2492178a98aa0ff3cd325e2d8", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::What Gmsh is pretty good at", "subcategory": "prose", "unit_id": "90806d127badcf4b587e49581c86cba6ea6375e7c0194408513bca632e385da9"}
